From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: mdt_loader: zero the bss when a user PD is reloaded

__qcom_mdt_load() zeroes the part of a segment that has no file data only
when the load is not done through the secure loader:

	if (!dma_required && phdr->p_memsz > phdr->p_filesz)
		memset(ptr + phdr->p_filesz, 0, phdr->p_memsz - phdr->p_filesz);

qcom_mdt_load_pd_seg(), the ASID-scoped reload an in-place user-PD restart
uses, passes dma_required = true, so that memset never runs for it. The
secure load copies the file-backed bytes of the segments it is given, and a
pure-BSS segment (p_filesz == 0) is not given to it at all. A reloaded PD
therefore starts on whatever the previous firmware left in its bss.

Measured on the RD03v2 bench (IPQ5018 + QCN6122), 2.4 GHz hw-restart with
the user-PD reload:

  [742.283] ... userpd trace: power-up complete id=1
  [752.487] ath11k c000000.wifi: failed to enable PMF QOS: (-108
  [752.499] Hardware became unavailable during restart.
  [752.504] WARNING: ... ieee80211_reconfig+0xb88/0x1070 [mac80211]
  [754.865] remoteproc remoteproc0: crash detected in q6wcss: type fatal error

The PD spawns and reports ready, but no chip_id/fw_version line follows, so
its QMI server never came up: ath11k then waits out its firmware start, the
WMI sends keep failing with -ESHUTDOWN because CRASH_FLUSH is still set, and
the root Q6 takes a fatal error ten seconds later. Segment 12 of ASID 1 is
757760 bytes of pure bss at 0x4b7aa000 that the reload never touched.

Zero the bss tail for both paths. The cold-boot behaviour is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
---
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/mdt_loader.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/mdt_loader.c
@@ -487,7 +487,14 @@
 				break;
 		}
 
-		if (!dma_required && phdr->p_memsz > phdr->p_filesz)
+		/*
+		 * Zero the bss tail on both paths. The secure segment load copies
+		 * only the file-backed bytes, and a pure-BSS segment (p_filesz ==
+		 * 0) is not sent to it at all, so a reloaded user PD would
+		 * otherwise start on the previous firmware's bss: it spawns and
+		 * reports ready, but never brings its QMI server up.
+		 */
+		if (phdr->p_memsz > phdr->p_filesz)
 			memset(ptr + phdr->p_filesz, 0, phdr->p_memsz - phdr->p_filesz);
 	}
 
